From d0a64c95f6e37a421ffc26652b1572473ccbca49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:43:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: eight contexts instead of four

The four contexts are shared by the decoder and the encoder nodes: the
fifth open() of either fails with -EBUSY. Android's codec list for
this driver advertises four decoder and four encoder instances, and the
vendor driver for the same MFC (drivers/media/platform/exynos/mfc)
allows 32. The limit only sizes dev->ctx[] and the bits of
ctx_work_bits, an unsigned long.

Use eight. With the 16 MiB pool on MFC v10, four H.264 or HEVC decoders
(2 MiB of context each) and four encoders fit together.

---
 drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
index c8113ce659..84aa14d067 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
 /* MFC definitions */
 #define MFC_MAX_EXTRA_DPB       5
 #define MFC_MAX_BUFFERS		32
-#define MFC_NUM_CONTEXTS	4
+#define MFC_NUM_CONTEXTS	8
 /* Interrupt timeout */
 #define MFC_INT_TIMEOUT		2000
 /* Busy wait timeout */
